        "Hidetoshi Katori",
        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks combine exceptional precision with a profound new capability to compare time, gravity, and fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Katori originated the magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, while Ye made decisive experimental realizations and broad precision applications.",
        "maturity": "Independent clock platforms now attain extraordinary and reproducible performance, with a long record of quantitative validation.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "A final award would need to define the boundary between the foundational clock concept and the wider precision-metrology community."
        ]
      }
    },
